Description: Vietnamese input method editor (Telex, VNI, VIQR) for IBus and Fcitx5
 TextVN converts keystrokes into Vietnamese with tone marks (Telex, VNI, VIQR
 and Simple Telex styles) using a shared Rust engine on Windows, macOS and
 Linux. This package provides the IBus engine, the Fcitx5 addon (installed to
 the multiarch addon directory), and the GTK4 settings application.
 .
 Highlights: old/new tone placement styles, output charsets (precomposed and
 decomposed Unicode, TCVN3, VNI Windows), macro/emoji expansion, English
 auto-restore with a 3000-word frequency dictionary, and Tab completion for
 Vietnamese syllables.
 .
 The input method integrates with the session's input-method framework: it is
 loaded by the host ibus-daemon or fcitx5 process, so it is not sandboxable
 inside Flatpak/Snap (see /usr/share/doc/textvn/user-guide.md).
